### Priority

Priority is **AI-determined** using the priority matrix. Never ask the user for priority.

| Condition | Priority |

|-----------|----------|

| User says "blocker" | Highest |

| Functional failure (feature broken, wrong result) | Highest |

| Processual failure (wrong flow, incorrect status) | Highest |

| Data integrity or security issue | Highest |

| Feature partially broken — workaround exists | High |

| Non-critical edge case, minor wrong behavior | Medium |

| Cosmetic / label / text / alignment | Low |

| No functional impact | Lowest |

---

### Bug template rules

- **Summary format:** `[Backend/Frontend] - <Component> - <Short problem>`

- **Section order (mandatory):**

  1. Summary

  2. Description (short context paragraph)

  3. Steps to reproduce

  4. Actual result

  5. Expected result

  6. **Environment** (BEFORE Technical details)

  7. Technical details (with Endpoint, Payload, Response, Status)

  8. Example

- **No Browser field** anywhere in the template

- **Environment section** always appears before Technical details — violation is a **MUST**

- **Technical details** section is mandatory for all API bugs; may be omitted only for pure UI/visual bugs with no API call

- All content in English (Rule 0.7)

